issue(id="0025" status="open")
  title Keep Renovate lockfiles compatible with frozen pnpm installs
  user-story
    as-a Package maintainer
    i-want Renovate npm updates to produce lockfiles accepted by CI.
    so-that Dependency updates can build, test, and merge automatically.
  premise.
    Renovate ignores pnpm hooks by default and removes pnpmfileChecksum when
    regenerating the lockfile. CI loads the existing hook and rejects the result.
    The hook's TypeScript 6 workaround targets tsdown 0.22 and Vite+ core 0.2;
    neither is in the current dependency graph, which uses tsdown 0.23.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion A lockfile regenerated with Renovate's hook policy passes a frozen install.
    criterion npm library declarations build with TypeScript 7 without the legacy hook.
    criterion CI runs the lockfile regression test and retains frozen installs.
  review-items
    item(status="open") Confirm CI passes with the obsolete hook removed.
